      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The downtown core of Como is listed on the National Historic Register, preserving its historic architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Como%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Como grew into a commercial hub thanks to the railroad that ran straight through the town center in the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://panolacounty.com/panola-overview/como/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s historic churches include Holy Innocent’s Episcopal Church, home to an authentic Tiffany window, and the domed Como United Methodist Church.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://panolacounty.com/panola-overview/como/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Como has produced several notable blues musicians, including Mississippi Fred McDowell, RL Boyce, and Othar Turner.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Como%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Over recent decades, Como has transitioned from a farming community to an artist community celebrated for its blues heritage and cultural events.",
